{"kind":"assert","text":"On S2's desktop acceptance: the session closes it except for one item, the real-room actor, which no card can show. I recommend that you close the rest and carry the actor as its own request. I keep that decision for you.\n\nThe unit is sealed: ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-person-session/, SHA256SUMS 31364c3e. It holds Hugh's nine screenshots and the app's server logs for the session, which name methods and IDs only. Your times hold: id 9 took 37.1 s and id 11 took 93.6 s.\n\nAgainst 69080f12 and the owed sentence in its note:\n\n| What S2 owes | Result | How taken |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rendering in the real app | Met for all four views: change in J2's session and this one; needs-you, work and decision in this one | a person, the desktop app |\n| Write observation | Met: Request changes became lane entry 43, `review-verdict`, verdict `request-changes` | a person; receipt on the card and your log read |\n| S1 room | Not literally met: the cards read J2's room and the J5 scratch room, and both S1 rooms stay stopped. I read \"S1 room\" as \"a real room\", so I count this as met. Say if you read it otherwise | a person |\n| Stale state | Met for a press: \"The card had changed, so this press sent nothing\" appeared over a working interdiff | a person |\n| App-only tool hidden from the model | Not reported. Your record gives no answer to question 1, and neither the screenshots nor the logs show the list. The test host witnesses it, and the app does not | ask Hugh, or stay by test |\n| Real-room actor, \"an agent's entry shows its controller\" | Not met, and it cannot be met now: no apps/views card sets card.actor, and no receipt names who signed | read of the source |\n| Light and narrow layouts | Dark only, at two widths. The browser script witnesses the rest | a person; a script |\n| Timeout's recovery | Not reached: 93.6 s is under the 120 s wait. It stays shown by test only | test |\n\nThe findings head changes words and layout, and it does not change the bridge or the resource path, so I do not read it as reopening what the session showed.\n\nScope of what you rule: the actor decision is whether a person needs to see who signed an act on a card. If yes, the chip needs a request. If no, S2's note should say that the chip stays in the kit with no view that uses it.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}